                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "agenres"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4a635586-a360-4d3f-9f5a-4123c61a9bc5",
                        "entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "agender"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0a2b8818-7606-4a2c-85a9-459d99d109ef",
                        "entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "tags": [
                            "Très rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "agenræ"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                        "entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sans genre, sans identité de genre. Une personne agenre ne ressent pas de genre. Il est possible qu'une personne agenre se reconnaisse aussi comme personne non-binaire et/ou transgenre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Genres humains et identités de genre",
                            "Non-binarité"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e394df5-d654-4e4e-8734-f12ee11a0dc3",
                                "sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                                "text": "Je me considère donc comme agenre et cis. Ceci n'a pas vocation à dire aux autres personnes agenres qu'elles n'ont pas légitimité à se considérer trans, mais simplement à expliquer mon point de vue sur le sujet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cae0bd3a-c4ba-44eb-b1e4-78d9709e5688",
                                "sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                                "text": "Agenre, ça veut dire que je ne suis ni un homme, ni une femme, ni entre les deux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca380f13-915c-44e3-aac2-76f792b00fae",
                                "sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                                "text": "Quand un membre du Collège veut renouveler son adhésion, on lui demande s’il est:\n– Féminin\n– Masculin\n– Agenre\n– Non conforme à un genre\n– De genre fluide\n– Non-binaire\n– Transmasculin\n– Transféminin\n– Bispirituel(le)\n– Bigenre\n– Cisgenre\n– De genre multiple\n– Autre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2f74c0b6-9552-40a8-80b1-873fe76ea537",
                        "source_entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "source_sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                        "target_lang_word": "agender",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agender",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                        "entry_id": "0bc53fa2-0867-3fed-8be2-0f8546dd6c35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without an associated gender (in any sense); not having a particular gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed9eb6dc-cc9c-410f-a935-6b520b35b8f9",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "An agender noun includes both the masculine and feminine forms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb9f9f90-04e5-4102-b785-6c32a103fb9d",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "All I understand is that G-d is amorphous, agender, etc. so \"image\" can't be a physical or gender or sexual thing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd09151e-145b-4f73-902a-b06d36346a53",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "\"He\" has been used as the default pronoun, and as I said, unfortunately there is no agender equivalent to he/she, as \"it\" is usually equated with something without life, or at least of a life form considered to be less intelligent (that in itself is negotiable, but this is for a different topic)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae671dbd-c01e-4bf3-988a-3845b9f62f96",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "But despite this near-universality of gender, cultures can have transgender, agender, and hypergender individuals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bca068f4-60e6-4bc7-8ac2-ff4bb9425094",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "There are faculty advisers on El’s theater crew who balk at using “they” for one person; classmates at El’s public school on the outskirts of Boston who insist El can’t be “multiple people”; and commenters on El’s social media feeds who dismiss nonbinary gender identities like androgyne (a combination of masculine and feminine), agender (the absence of gender) and gender-fluid (moving between genders) as lacking a basis in biology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa0e903e-a66f-45a8-b1ea-2b1715c435eb",
                                                "sense_id": "bf570d97-1a5b-3a77-910e-ef6283a8150f",
                                                "text": "\"'Agender'? I'm pretty sure that means not identifying as a particular gender? I'm sorry. That's just what it made me think of. I'm not trying to tell you what to--\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e1c68f62-c76a-44c6-b6ae-7bce73cc9a4d",
                        "source_entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "source_sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                        "target_lang_word": "genderless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "genderless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8204c37-d13d-3a42-9699-5c7355270091",
                                        "entry_id": "cba2ee90-d020-3f15-9c63-b52577c81a65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without a gender, in its various senses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18a200b9-62c3-40d6-bdf9-7274d25de1b2",
                                                "sense_id": "a8204c37-d13d-3a42-9699-5c7355270091",
                                                "text": "A genderless noun includes both the masculine and feminine forms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9b56fc7-bb31-49bf-8ae4-721443607241",
                                                "sense_id": "a8204c37-d13d-3a42-9699-5c7355270091",
                                                "text": "Should retailers promote genderless shopping?... Through its Agender concept store, Selfridges is selling clothing, accessories and beauty supplies that, it says, \"transcend notions of 'his' and 'hers'.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "86882896-0dd2-4fd6-85cc-c2c577380eee",
                        "source_entry_id": "b26d2fdc-c8a8-35d3-9231-f604edf9b238",
                        "source_sense_id": "490f6440-fb14-3019-be57-07684da1cd2c",
                        "target_lang_word": "gender-free",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gender-free",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efbc1912-94d6-3c65-b6e1-af3b23508e94",
                                        "entry_id": "9e294bbd-5440-3e8f-95a2-c3366daa3948",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Agender, being neither male nor female nor any third gender; free of gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of people"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "210a3898-95a5-4e40-802c-e179f33906c1",
                                                "sense_id": "efbc1912-94d6-3c65-b6e1-af3b23508e94",
                                                "text": "When we rendezvous shortly thereafter, I learn that the box office is being manned, if that's the right word, by an odd-looking grizzled entity unknown to my wife but whom I infer from her description (and soon after confirm) to be the genderfree or ambigendered \"Ditsy\" from Maintenance, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b981976-bba1-4d43-be4c-7c545c318044",
                                                "sense_id": "efbc1912-94d6-3c65-b6e1-af3b23508e94",
                                                "text": "Individuals holding these views challenge the existing Western binary and categorical sex-gender system, increasingly identifying as bigender, gender blender, or gender-free."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01df338b-d7fa-4db0-8285-a545f8e92b17",
                                                "sense_id": "efbc1912-94d6-3c65-b6e1-af3b23508e94",
                                                "text": "I began thinking of myself as a gender-free person."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                        "entry_id": "9e294bbd-5440-3e8f-95a2-c3366daa3948",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Acceptable for or available to any gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of words"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3ca0937-c815-465d-96e7-bf2e8df4d458",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "He got the idea of transforming the traditional sashiko — quilted-cotton worker's pants and jacket fabric — into a modern leisure fabric, a homegrown equivalent of denim, which became another early source of gender-free clothing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b63131c3-b095-4db3-941b-d1d8bb3ca03a",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "The term ‘engineer’ is apparently a gender-free term - there is no single word meaning ‘female engineer’ - but it seems to contain an invisible male marking. ‘Nurse’ works in the opposite way, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac09ac83-7593-4d72-9b21-95ab968f166d",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "In the German, Buber often used the term Mensch, a gender-free term, which is best translated as person or human being. In contrast, the term Mann does refer to a male person."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3349793-9dea-4314-bc93-7fcd3e5e6822",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "During the same decades in which feminist critiques of generic uses of “man” and “he” led to widespread changes in usage — no mean feat — \"you guys” became even more widely accepted as an informal and allegedly gender-free phrase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "920faea3-1ed7-46b5-9755-6dac8e146b39",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "Tabyi-daw, Hiroko Kawanami observes, is a gender-free term of self-address used when speaking to monks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f4d2d24-6e6d-40f4-a2e1-3f94696793b8",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "Sometime in the early Seventies, gender-free toys were briefly a popular idea. So at Christmas on the California beach in 1972, we downplayed the dolls with frilly dresses and loaded up Santa's sack with toy trucks and earth movers for our three daughters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9a781fd-17d8-42b7-8a97-22319bceaafd",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "Well, liberation has made retirement a gender-free option, and we are facing not only the notion of fixing lunch every day, but also of eating it alone. Which is a large part of the problem."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d88d4e4b-40ab-43f0-8656-a8fa0180bbe1",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bc03b9-4f87-31d9-a483-1490f020eabd",
                                                "text": "Gender-free toys. Let children of either sex play with the dolls, houses, tea sets, blocks, trucks, and fireman's hats however they choose. Your little girl may grow up to be an engineer or an anthropologist, and your little boy may become the most exquisite chef."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                        "entry_id": "9e294bbd-5440-3e8f-95a2-c3366daa3948",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Which does not define people on the basis of gender; in which gender is irrelevant to people's lives and choices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a society"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e0de3aa-8e45-42ff-b1b7-6f0eec01df97",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                                "text": "So once the notion of a gender-free society is clarified, there should be widespread agreement [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c54df686-d9ba-40db-8be5-c3def6164763",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                                "text": "Many argue that we must build a gender-free world, that is, a world in which society does not define and organize all people on the basis of gender categories."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "932752a2-f09c-449c-b475-fa42c50cd7e2",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                                "text": "The underlying argument is that if gender relations were altered at the level of social structure (ie, in the social institutions of the family, workplace, state policies, the courts, and media), a more gender-free world would eventually lead to gender-free parenting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ab5b349-7f43-48b6-b5bd-79d5c79fcdd5",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                                "text": "Do you think a child raised in a relatively gender-free environment will develop differently from other children?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d40b826-03c2-4c59-a1a0-5da2645ad2db",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd4afaa-6ab7-30ed-a952-69384fb75903",
                                                "text": "Japanese reformers speak of ‘gender-free’ situations as the goal of reform. [...] A gender-free society remains a useful conceptual benchmark for thinking about change."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
